  "name": "edit: enforce state-transition legality and state<->session coherence on hand-edits",
  "slug": "edit-enforce-state-transition-legality-and-state-session-coh",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "slop edit validates schema+edges+ancestry+id-immutability but not state-transition legality or state/active_session coupling. A hand-edit can install an out-of-order state (open->done, skipping review and the done-cascade) or an incoherent pairing (state:done with active_session still set), and a later slop stop then resurrects the done ticket to open.",
    "details_md": "",
    "acceptance": [
      "If the edited state differs from before, route it through the same legality checks the dedicated commands use (or reject entering/leaving in_progress/review/done/dropped via edit)",
      "Add an active_session<->state coherence check (session-carrying states require a live active_session; open/draft/terminal require null)",
      "Tests cover an out-of-order state edit and an incoherent state/session edit being rejected"
    ],
    "context": [
      "src/cli/commands/edit.ts:127-182",
      "src/tickets/edit.ts:29-43 validateEditedTicketText (schema+id only)",
      "src/core/entities/ticket.ts:94 active_session independent of state"
    ],
